-#
-#  Kaminari theme "wsjrdp" -- the pager of shared/wsjrdp/_expandable_table_paging,
-#  which asks for it with `theme: "wsjrdp", left: 1, right: 1`. Kaminari looks
-#  every tag partial of a themed paginator up under kaminari/wsjrdp/ alone, with
-#  no fallback to kaminari/, so the theme ships each partial it uses.
-#
-#  Layout:  [<] [>] 1 ... 30 31 32 33 [34] 35 36 37 38 ... 137
-#    * the two step buttons come FIRST and are ALWAYS rendered (disabled on the
-#      first resp. last page, see _prev_page/_next_page), so paging on stays a
-#      row of clicks in one place -- neither their own position nor that of the
-#      numbers behind them depends on where in the range the current page is.
-#    * no first/last tag: `left: 1, right: 1` turns page 1 and the last page
-#      into ordinary number links, and the gap tag bridges the rest.
= paginator.render do
  %ul.pagination.pagination-sm
    = prev_page_tag
    = next_page_tag
    - each_page do |page|
      - if page.left_outer? || page.right_outer? || page.inside_window?
        = page_tag page
      - elsif !page.was_truncated?
        = gap_tag
